WEBVTT

00:00:01.866 --> 00:00:04.632
-[Narrator] Welcome to Module 2 Accessible Microsoft Word

00:00:04.633 --> 00:00:07.833
Documents. In this video, you will learn how to

00:00:07.833 --> 00:00:10.066
make your Microsoft Word documents accessible to

00:00:10.066 --> 00:00:10.832
all learners.

00:00:12.933 --> 00:00:15.866
In this section, we will set your document title

00:00:15.866 --> 00:00:16.599
and language.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.766
To set a document title in Microsoft Word, you will

00:00:21.766 --> 00:00:26.166
click File, then select Info. From the right-hand

00:00:26.166 --> 00:00:29.699
panel, locate the Properties section. Click on the

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.833
space indicated to the right of Title. Enter a

00:00:31.833 --> 00:00:35.733
descriptive title here, such as "Accessibility

00:00:35.866 --> 00:00:38.566
Training Module 1.0."

00:00:41.333 --> 00:00:44.033
To set the document language, go to the Review tab.

00:00:44.766 --> 00:00:47.732
Select Language, and choose Set Proofing Language.

00:00:48.866 --> 00:00:51.432
From the list, select your desired language, such

00:00:51.433 --> 00:00:55.033
as English (United States). Check the box labeled,

00:00:55.366 --> 00:00:58.799
"Do not check spelling or grammar," and then click

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:02.833
OK to apply your settings. Now your document has

00:01:02.833 --> 00:01:04.933
a title that will assist the screen reader in

00:01:04.933 --> 00:01:07.433
announcing the title and document clearly, and

00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:09.599
proper document language to pronounce words

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:12.066
correctly and ensure assistive technologies

00:01:12.066 --> 00:01:13.699
deliver your content accurately.

00:01:15.833 --> 00:01:18.799
In this section, we will use Word Styles and

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:23.033
review hyperlinks for accessibility. Let's

00:01:23.033 --> 00:01:25.499
structure a document with accessible hyperlinks,

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:28.766
clear headings, and properly formatted lists so

00:01:28.766 --> 00:01:32.166
screen readers can navigate with ease. To insert

00:01:32.166 --> 00:01:34.999
an accessible hyperlink, we need to ensure that it

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:38.733
is clear and actionable and not just a link. Start

00:01:38.733 --> 00:01:41.299
by selecting Insert from the menu, followed by the

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:45.200
Links tab. From that dropdown menu, you will select

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:48.900
Link. Then, another dropdown menu will appear;

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:53.700
select Insert Link from the bottom of that menu. A

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:57.200
window pops up to customize your hyperlink. Paste

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.733
the link in the space indicated to the right of

00:01:59.733 --> 00:02:03.266
Address at the bottom of the window. The important

00:02:03.266 --> 00:02:05.799
part is at the top of the window, where you will

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:08.833
enter a descriptive title such as, "Visit the

00:02:08.833 --> 00:02:13.366
Library Website" instead of "Click Here." "Visit the

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:15.732
Library Website" alerts someone listening to a

00:02:15.733 --> 00:02:18.133
screen reader that there is an actionable item in

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:18.699
the document.

00:02:21.966 --> 00:02:24.666
Rather than just changing the font size, it is

00:02:24.666 --> 00:02:26.866
important to apply true heading style.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:31.833
Start at the Home tab, open the Styles group, and

00:02:31.833 --> 00:02:34.199
select the heading level that fits your document

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:38.400
structure. For example, use Heading 1 for your

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:43.033
main title, Heading 2 for your major sections, and

00:02:43.033 --> 00:02:44.699
Heading 3 for your sub-sections.

00:02:50.766 --> 00:02:53.999
Bulleted or numbered lists should be formatted from

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.166
the Paragraph group. Choose your list type from

00:02:57.166 --> 00:03:02.799
the dropdown menu: bullet, numbered, or multilevel.

00:03:05.266 --> 00:03:08.366
For lists, always use a bulleted or numbered list

00:03:08.366 --> 00:03:10.766
tool instead of typing symbols manually.

00:03:14.333 --> 00:03:17.033
In this section, we will fix the color contrast

00:03:17.033 --> 00:03:21.899
issue and make the table accessible. Design

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:24.866
choices can make or break accessibility. With color

00:03:24.866 --> 00:03:27.299
contrast, text should clearly stand out from the

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:31.333
background, at least a 4.5 to 1 ratio for normal

00:03:31.333 --> 00:03:35.099
text. These are a few tips to keep in mind: Word's

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:37.733
default theme colors, black text on white

00:03:37.733 --> 00:03:40.433
background, already meet accessibility contrast

00:03:40.433 --> 00:03:41.066
requirements.

00:03:44.266 --> 00:03:46.432
Adding a table to your document always requires

00:03:46.433 --> 00:03:50.733
using the Insert tab from the menu. Do not draw or

00:03:50.733 --> 00:03:53.933
paste a table from another program. When you

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:56.999
insert your table from the Table menu tab, always

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:00.333
add clear header row and column data so screen

00:04:00.333 --> 00:04:02.766
readers can identify columns in context.

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:11.033
Remember, accessibility isn't just compliance, 

00:04:11.033 --> 00:04:14.166
it's clarity. Your students benefit when content

00:04:14.166 --> 00:04:16.966
is easy to see, follow, and understand.

00:04:21.033 --> 00:04:24.033
In this section, we will add alternative text to

00:04:24.033 --> 00:04:25.499
images and other objects.

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:30.199
When using images or graphics, always

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:34.700
include alternative text or alt text. For students

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:37.500
requiring a screen reader, alt text provides

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:39.866
assistive technologies a description of the image

00:04:39.866 --> 00:04:43.299
represented in the document. This is especially

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:46.733
helpful for students with visual impairments. Be

00:04:46.733 --> 00:04:48.866
sure to keep the description concise but

00:04:48.866 --> 00:04:52.366
meaningful. If no alt text is provided of a chart

00:04:52.366 --> 00:04:55.932
or graph, for example, the screen reader will only

00:04:55.933 --> 00:04:59.599
say, "Image of a chart." This is useless for a

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:02.700
visually impaired student. Rather, inserting a

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:06.333
description like, "Chart showing enrollment

00:05:06.333 --> 00:05:08.899
increases by 20% over five years."

00:05:11.833 --> 00:05:16.399
For SmartArt, charts, and equations, right-click and

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:20.600
select Edit Alt Text to describe what's shown. If

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:23.000
the visual is decorative, mark it as such.

00:05:26.433 --> 00:05:29.066
Accessible visuals ensure no learner misses the

00:05:29.066 --> 00:05:30.799
message your content conveys.

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:36.533
In this section, we will run the accessibility

00:05:36.533 --> 00:05:39.499
checker and do a quick manual review for accessibility.

00:05:41.033 --> 00:05:45.899
Once your document is complete, go to the Review tab and click Check Accessibility.

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:49.900
The inspection panel will show errors, warnings,

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:54.466
and tips. While the inspection panel shows issues

00:05:54.466 --> 00:05:57.766
like missing alt text, hard to read color

00:05:57.766 --> 00:06:01.566
contrast warning, or table using merged/split cells

00:06:01.566 --> 00:06:04.699
warnings, it does not include all requirements by

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:06.933
the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines.

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:11.833
Therefore, it is important to manually review your

00:06:11.833 --> 00:06:14.766
document content to identify and fix accessibility

00:06:14.766 --> 00:06:17.399
issues the checker may miss.

00:06:19.533 --> 00:06:21.799
Headers and footers should not include essential

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:24.500
information because most screen readers may not

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:27.900
navigate to those areas. As a result, users who

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:30.133
rely on them may miss important content.
